id: pm-github-vhi6
title: Bound coverage aggregation memory and compare default-heap CI behavior
description: "During the PR #122 privacy-scope regression work, an identity-isolated npm release:check completed 587/587 tests with zero failures, skips or cancellations, then c8 report aggregation exhausted Node's default 4 GiB heap. Native coverage receipts occupied approximately 2.9 GiB. The security fix is being validated with NODE_OPTIONS=--max-old-space-size=12288 and unchanged source inventory and four 100-percent thresholds. Compare default-heap CI behavior, investigate bounded report aggregation or documented resource requirements, and retain complete authored-source and real CLI coverage. Earlier local heap-exhaustion observations also appear in pm-github-fmrf; this task tracks current default-heap acceptance separately from the scope fix in pm-github-wrmt."
type: Task
status: open
priority: 2
tags[4]: changelog-unreleased,coverage,follow-up,gates
created_at: "2026-10-14T14:32:34.672Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-03T12:30:03.134Z"
author: codex-agent
comments[21]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-14T15:04:27.090Z",codex-agent,"Confirmed resource workaround: complete identity-isolated npm and Bun release:check each passed 587/587 tests and all 11 checks with NODE_OPTIONS=--max-old-space-size=12288. Coverage remains exact 100/100/100/100 across 12 authored modules, without source exemptions or threshold changes. The earlier default-heap npm run passed all 587 tests before c8 aggregation exhausted the heap. Default-heap CI comparison and bounded aggregation remain follow-up work; the security change does not alter coverage implementation or CI memory settings."
  "2026-10-24T14:34:24.911Z",codex-agent,"Additional measured receipt from pm-github-closeout-attribution / PR 174: CI https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/actions/runs/40101464708 at 30b94f1 failed all four npm/Bun release jobs on Node 22/26 with JavaScript heap exhaustion during c8 aggregation at the existing 8192 MiB limit. The Node 26 test phases each passed 1337/1337, zero failures/cancellations/skips before aggregation failed. No release-gate pass is claimed. This round reduces repeated setup in the new 36-case workflow matrix (shared immutable Git/tracker baselines and only the actual closeout/publication steps); the broader bounded aggregation task remains open, with thresholds, source inventory and heap configuration unchanged."
  "2026-10-24T15:10:00.744Z",codex-agent,"Second receipt: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/actions/runs/40103921945 at ad2e7cb passed 1337/1337 tests in every npm/Bun Node 22/26 job, then all four c8 aggregations exhausted the unchanged 8192 MiB heap. Sharing tracker callers alone was insufficient while package setup still repeated per cell. The next harness prepares package/scope setup once per immutable baseline; every one of the 36 cases still restores input, runs actual branch preparation, real CLI closeout, publication privacy/refusal gates and leased push, with fresh receipts and provenance/history assertions. No coverage resource or threshold change is used. The broader bounded aggregation task remains open."
  "2026-10-24T15:38:04.069Z",codex-agent,"Third CI https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/actions/runs/40106191758 at cff0f1c passed the complete npm release gate on Node 22 after preparing four baseline callers once. Both Node 26 jobs still passed 1337/1337 tests and exhausted c8 at 8192 MiB. Fixture reductions alone cannot establish Node 26 full-gate acceptance. Adjust only the c8 merge heap ceiling to 12288 MiB, leaving headroom on this public repository's documented 16 GB ubuntu-latest runners (https://docs.github.com/en/actions/reference/runners/github-hosted-runners#standard-github-hosted-runners-for-public-repositories). All four coverage thresholds remain 100, the complete 19-module inventory, zero-exclusion policy, test set and dependency pins stay unchanged. Earlier comments preserving the 8 GiB ceiling describe failed earlier attempts; measured Node 26 failures now justify this resource-only revision. General bounded aggregation remains unfinished and this item will not be closed."
  "2026-10-24T15:42:23.333Z",codex-agent,"Resource-only local verification: PM-linked node --test test/coverage-gate.test.ts passes 9/9, zero failures/cancellations/skips. These tests run real c8 fixture reports and preserve threshold-refusal, missing-source, invalid-receipt and pre-entry heap-routing controls. Production typecheck, test typecheck, lint, docstrings and zero duplication pass. Only COVERAGE_HEAP_FLAG changes from 8192 to 12288 MiB, plus explanatory comments. Full CI is still required; this is not bounded-memory certification and the general task stays in progress for orchestrator follow-up."
  "2026-10-24T21:53:34.277Z",codex-agent,"Returned to open in the 2026-10-24 sweep: PR 174 reduces fixture duplication and raises the c8 heap limit, but explicitly leaves bounded coverage aggregation unfinished. No active work."
  "2026-11-02T13:08:38.050Z",codex-sol,"Additional #175 gate receipt: the expanded 1609-case full suite reached c8 aggregation, which exhausted the unchanged 12288 MiB cap. Test failures were separately corrected on pm-github-repeat-noop; no gate pass is claimed from this attempt. Checking an operational NODE_OPTIONS=--max-old-space-size-percentage=60 override, which Node documents as taking precedence over the explicit absolute cap. No source inventory, threshold, exclusion, assertion or checked-in heap default is changed; bounded/default-cap aggregation remains open."
  "2026-11-02T13:17:42.367Z",codex-sol,"Resource probe completed successfully: c8 can aggregate the retained first-attempt native receipts with NODE_OPTIONS=--max-old-space-size-percentage=60, preserving the checked-in 12288 MiB argument. This is only a memory-capacity probe, not corrected-source coverage certification: the retained run had three test failures and source changed afterwards. A new complete release:check now reruns all tests and exact four-dimensional 100-percent gates with that operational override. No gate source or assertion changes. Default-cap CI/resource acceptance remains open."
  "2026-11-02T17:44:18.578Z",codex-sol,"Continuation resource receipt for #175: fresh complete release:check now exits 0 with operational NODE_OPTIONS=--max-old-space-size-percentage=60. Tests 1609/1609, exact 100/100/100/100 across 28 authored modules (13197 lines/statements, 422 functions, 5075 branches), zero skipped source. The checked-in 12288 MiB ceiling and all gate thresholds/exclusions remain unchanged. This demonstrates current-source local acceptance with the operational override only; bounded aggregation and default-cap CI remain unresolved. Item stays open."
  "2026-11-03T01:03:42.261Z",codex-sol,"Claimed on the requested main base. Plan: measure unmodified raw receipts and timed c8 aggregation first; inspect c8 12 implementation, retain the exact inventory and four complete coverage dimensions, add a filter-safety mutation proof if filtering is needed, then run the final release gate serially. CI evidence: PR #213 run 41533314090 passed 1609 tests in Node 22/26 before the 12288 MiB merge heap exhausted; main run 41541407120 narrowly passed. No source exemptions or test removals are authorized."
  "2026-11-03T01:04:27.347Z",codex-sol,"c8 12.0.0 source inspection confirms parse-args.js supports --merge-async and report.js _getMergedProcessCovAsync reads one file, normalizes it, and merges it into a running accumulator. The default _loadReports instead retains all parsed receipts; --exclude-after-remap also retains non-inventory scripts until conversion. First candidate is the native incremental merge, before adding any custom filtering. Installation completed with the mandated clean npm user configuration; baseline coverage is running serially after memory and disk checks."
  "2026-11-03T01:16:24.614Z",codex-sol,"Interim baseline sample (not final): 263 raw receipts totaled 757325680 bytes; included script entries were 420651 serialized bytes, excluded script entries 709267946 bytes, and excluded source-map payloads 47447444 bytes. The baseline still runs the unchanged full workflow suite; final counts and timed peak RSS will follow after all children exit. There is no NODE_OPTIONS override."
  "2026-11-03T03:25:33.386Z",codex-sol,"Unchanged baseline test phase completed: 1609 tests, 1607 passes, two failures, zero skips/cancellations. Both failures are existing privacy tests reporting an unrelated unreachable commit identity in the shared Git object store, tracked separately in pm-github-privacy-store-followup. The whole-store gate and identity allowlist remain unchanged. The baseline c8 merge is still being timed. Final release acceptance will run in an independent clone of this branch, with full local-store privacy scope inside that clone; shared-store health remains a separate limitation."
  "2026-11-03T03:34:00.548Z",codex-sol,"Final unchanged-run raw inventory: coverage/v8 contains 3839 JSON receipts totaling 10074310347 bytes; maximum receipt 6701513 bytes. JSON-serialized script entries matching the 28 authored-source file URLs: 1268 entries / 4689282 bytes. Outside those raw URLs: 1981178 entries / 9004210507 bytes. Cached source-map value payloads: 0 included bytes / 1059962540 excluded bytes. Remaining bytes are JSON framing, URL keys and metadata; raw URL classification is before remapping. The default c8 merge remains near its 12288 MiB ceiling; peak timing is pending."
  "2026-11-03T03:37:21.066Z",codex-sol,"Unmodified baseline merge reproduced the heap failure after the completed test phase: FATAL ERROR: Ineffective mark-compacts near heap limit. /usr/bin/time -v on npm run coverage recorded maximum RSS 12798016 KiB and exit 1 with the unchanged --max-old-space-size=12288. Test failures were only the two separate shared-store privacy controls. The incremental replay now uses exactly those 3839 raw receipts, the same --all/include/remap/report options, --merge-async and a 6144 MiB heap cap, after fresh memory/disk checks (17 GiB available, 112 GB free)."
  "2026-11-03T04:11:05.980Z",codex-sol,"Native incremental replay of the same 3839 receipts finished without heap exhaustion: peak RSS 1632684 KiB (1.557 GiB), versus 12798016 KiB (12.205 GiB) before. The replay reports 13197/13197 lines and statements, 422/422 functions, and 5077/5078 branches; the sole uncovered privacy CLI branch corresponds to the baseline's two shared-store privacy failures. No passing full gate is claimed from this replay. Selected native --merge-async, retaining all remapping/inclusion behavior and every raw receipt; custom pre-filtering is unnecessary. The heap flag is now 3072 MiB, about 1.44 GiB above the measured peak RSS (a conservative upper bound for heap). Extending the existing real-c8 test with 512 synthetic excluded receipts under a 128 MiB merge heap, plus covered/uncovered-line and unloaded-module checks; no test files or source modules are added or excluded."
  "2026-11-03T04:15:51.571Z",codex-sol,"Regression verification passed 10/10 coverage-gate tests directly and through pm test --run --progress. The 512-receipt fixture serializes 158244352 bytes and passes with a 128 MiB merge heap. Removing only --merge-async reproduced a small-heap OOM and failed the many-receipt assertion. A separate c8 normalization mutation dropped source.ts only when its receipt contained a zero-count range; it failed the retained-covered-counter assertion. Both mutations were restored, then the linked test passed. Source inventory remains 28 modules and the full suite still contains 1609 tests. Measurement, margin, native-filter safety and reproduction commands are documented in docs/bounded-coverage-merge.md."
  "2026-11-03T07:00:28.017Z",codex-sol,"Final acceptance: the single NPM_CONFIG_USERCONFIG=/dev/null npm run release:check exited 0 in the independent candidate clone. All 1609 tests passed, zero failures/skips/cancellations. Exact coverage of the unchanged 28-module inventory: 13195/13195 lines and statements, 422/422 functions, 5080/5080 branches, zero skipped source. /usr/bin/time -v recorded peak RSS 1665096 KiB (1.588 GiB), exactly matching the observed c8 VmHWM, with --max-old-space-size=3072; margin to the heap ceiling is approximately 1.41 GiB. Final receipts: 3844 files / 10084268775 bytes. All source/test hashes were unchanged before/after validation. Typecheck, build, 261 documented declarations, lint, zero duplication, 3718-object privacy audit, zero production vulnerabilities, 75-file pack dry run, changelog check and publish attestation all passed. Both baseline privacy failures pass in the independent clone; the separate shared-store issue remains open. Hosted Node 22/26 CI is intentionally not awaited."
  "2026-11-03T09:08:14.061Z",claude-orchestrator,"CodeRabbit follow-up on 5f6a58c: the bounded-heap test compared the spawned flag with COVERAGE_HEAP_FLAG itself, so a changed ceiling passed. Added a literal assertion for --max-old-space-size=3072 (the value docs/bounded-coverage-merge.md documents). Mutation proof: setting the constant to 4096 fails the test 0/1; restored passes 1/1."
  "2026-11-03T11:15:32.849Z",claude-orchestrator,"CodeRabbit full review on f06c47c (Major): an inherited NODE_OPTIONS --max-old-space-size-percentage overrides the explicit 3072 MiB flag (measured 19406 vs 3264 MiB on this host). runCoverageGate now strips every inherited old-space limit from NODE_OPTIONS via withoutHeapOverrides, keeping other options. Tests: spy pins the sanitized env (fails 0/1 with the sanitizer removed), real-node probe bounds the effective limit; docs/bounded-coverage-merge.md updated."
  "2026-11-03T12:30:03.133Z",claude-orchestrator,"CodeRabbit round 3 on 6eea264: a double-quoted NODE_OPTIONS option (\"--max-old-space-size-percentage=60\") kept its quotes and escaped the override pattern. withoutHeapOverrides now tokenizes like Node (quoted parts with backslash escapes, anywhere in an option), judges the unquoted value and keeps unrelated options byte-for-byte. Tests: quoted percentage, quoted value, quoted unrelated --require/--title kept; matching the raw token instead fails 0/1."
